  "body": "## What changed\n\nPast the 1.2 M-cell / 40 M-claim budgets, the hidden-rest scan (`crates/sim/src/stock_sim/scan_hidden.rs`) used to read `RestUnjudged` (\"NOT JUDGED\") and block the post. It now gives a real verdict there:\n\n- **Streamed in row bands.** `cells` / `claims` now cap what one pass *holds* at once (the bins, ~1.6 GB at 40 M claims), not what the verdict can read. When a lattice doesn't fit, its claims are counted row by row, the rows are cut into bands that fit, and each band is judged by the **same** body. Every column sees the same claims, pairing and distance law, so the banded verdict matches the whole-lattice verdict bit for bit (rows go in ascending order and a tie keeps the first worst). Nothing is sampled coarser, because a skipped column could hide a ledge and a false clean is a gouge-class bug.\n- **Bounded work.** `ScanBudget` gains `work` (shipped 1 G facet-column visits plus ball-center distances, about 10 s at worst). The scan still answers `OverBudget` / NOT JUDGED by name past that limit, or when a single row's claims cannot be held. It never hangs and never reports a stated zero.\n- **Exact nearest-center query** (`scan_near.rs`, new). A uniform XY grid over the center path, walked ring by ring outward. The walk stops on the ring's XY lower bound combined with the path's Z-range gap. The previous query's segment is tried first. A top is let go early only when it provably cannot raise the worst rest, so the minimum is the same number a linear scan returns.\n\nDecision record: `docs/decisions/24-field-scan-verdict.md`. A coarse lattice was dropped because it is not conservative. Per-column SDF parity was dropped because it costs O(columns x facets).\n\n## Readings\n\n- 21-plate stack over 100 x 100 mm, r = 0.5 ball: 1.07 M columns and 44.0 M claims, which is past the shipped 40 M. **Before:** NOT JUDGED. **After:** judged, 41.206 mm hidden rest at the deepest plate top between two passes (hypot(10, 40.5) - 0.5, as expected). In release the verdict takes 14.5 s, of which 2.2 s is everything except the hidden half.\n- Ceiling fixture streamed at a 600-claim budget (it holds about 4096 claims): rest and location identical to the whole scan, bit for bit.\n\n## Pinning tests\n\n`crates/sim/tests/hidden_rest_banded.rs`:\n- `past_the_claim_budget_the_hidden_slab_is_still_found`: the hidden rest is found while streaming.\n- `past_the_cell_budget_the_bands_answer_too`\n- `a_small_hidden_ledge_in_one_band_is_not_skipped`: a localized ledge is found with tight bands.\n- `a_clean_flat_stays_clean_when_streamed`: the clean case.\n- `the_walk_stays_bounded_and_says_so`: the work cap still refuses by name.\n- `a_stack_past_the_shipped_budget_gets_a_real_verdict`: `#[ignore]` heavy lane (release). The 44 M-claim model under `ScanBudget::SHIPPED`, with a time bound.\n\n`crates/sim/tests/stock_sim.rs::hidden_rest_over_budget_says_not_judged` is updated: it now starves a single row (claims, cells) or the work budget.\n\n## Gate\n\n- `cargo clippy -p camcraft-sim --all-targets -- -D warnings`: clean.\n- All camcraft-sim suites in debug: green.\n- camcraft-motion `finish3d`, `flow`, `pivot5d`, `turning_blade`, `turning_form`, `turning_thread`: green.\n- camcraft-app `posed_contact`, `turning_form`, `turning_thread`, `verify`: green.\n- Release heavy lane: `hidden_rest_banded --ignored` green, motion `finish3d --ignored` 33/33 green (60.6 s).\n\nChangelog: The hidden-rest scan gives a real verdict past its 1.2 M-cell / 40 M-claim budget (streamed in row bands, same verdict bit for bit); only its new work budget still reads NOT JUDGED\n\nFixes #24\n\n🤖 Generated with [Claude Code](https://claude.com/claude-code)\n",
